21
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,600
How to Read an Order Flow Chart

22
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,834
An order flow chart allows a trader to see volume traded on

23
00:01:23,834 --> 00:01:26,259
the bid and the volume traded on the offer.

24
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:29,298
However, you can use range charts, minute charts, ranko charts,

25
00:01:29,298 --> 00:01:32,336
whatever type of chart you are comfortable looking at, order

26
00:01:32,336 --> 00:01:34,159
flow can be applied to it.

27
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:39,480
Whatever time range you look at, you can apply to it.

28
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,820
It doesn't necessarily have to be,

29
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:43,520
you know, a one minute chart,

30
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,786
a five minute chart, a five range chart,

31
00:01:45,786 --> 00:01:46,919
a ten range chart.

32
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,600
You can look at point and figures, you can look at ranko charts.

33
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:55,380
Whatever chart you're comfortable looking at and you're currently using, you can apply order flow to it.

34
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:58,820
That said, the chart should be on an intraday basis.

35
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:00,371
You know, looking

36
00:02:00,371 --> 00:02:02,356
at an order flow chart on a

37
00:02:02,356 --> 00:02:04,341
daily basis is kind of, I don't

38
00:02:04,341 --> 00:02:07,178
say useless, but I haven't found any value in it.

39
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,880
You know, you want to see the order flow as it's coming in.

40
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,008
If you're looking at a daily chart

41
00:02:13,008 --> 00:02:15,136
trying to discern the order flow, it's

42
00:02:15,136 --> 00:02:16,960
a mess because, you know, you're

43
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:23,040
basically trying to follow the order flow, but on a daily chart, you're just seeing a big dump of data.

44
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:24,511
When you spread it

45
00:02:24,511 --> 00:02:25,968
out over, you know, you break

46
00:02:25,968 --> 00:02:28,639
it down over the trading day, that's when it's most powerful.

47
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:31,700
So, what does an order flow chart look like?

48
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:38,480
Well, when you're in an order flow chart, you compare price on the bid against the offer diagonally, not horizontally.

49
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:43,740
So, you're comparing, you know, the 686 against 12.

50
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:47,040
It's what traded, not the bid and the offer.

51
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,100
The market's always going to have a bid and an offer.

52
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,460
What you want to do is compare the relationship.

53
00:02:52,720 --> 00:03:01,380
Again, what's important with order flows is you want to compare traded volume, not volume in the book.

54
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:05,840
So, when you see a footprint chart, it's the volume that's actually traded.

55
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,160
Why is that important?

56
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:12,460
Because that is what the, how people commit themselves to the market.

57
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:16,340
You know, when you work a bid and an offer and you're not getting filled, you're not committed.

58
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:19,540
When you trade, you're committed to the market. You have a position.

59
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:24,840
So, remember, there's always a bid and offer in the market. That's how trading is conducted.

60
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:30,920
Here you have the market, 913 and a quarter bid, 913 and a half offer.

61
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:32,760
The size on the bid is 280.

62
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:34,660
The size on the offer is 565.

63
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,002
If you want to buy at the market,

64
00:03:38,002 --> 00:03:40,684
you buy the offer. So, in this case,

65
00:03:40,684 --> 00:03:44,372
you would buy it at 19, 13, 15. You are considered to be aggressive.

66
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:52,460
If you want to sell at the market, you sell at the bid. And you are being aggressive as well.

67
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:56,700
Whenever you go to the price where the market is bid or offered, you are being aggressive.

68
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,755
If you're joining the bid or the offer, then

69
00:03:59,755 --> 00:04:02,270
you're being passive, which if you are content to

70
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:08,978
let the market come to you, then you'd work a bid if you want to buy or an offer if you want to sell.

71
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,320
Well, this is considered passive buying or selling.

72
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:14,675
When you're working a bid to buy or an offer to sell,

73
00:04:14,675 --> 00:04:18,898
there's no guarantee that you'll get filled, even if price trades at the price you are working at.

74
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:24,284
Order flow charts monitor not just the volume

75
00:04:24,284 --> 00:04:26,274
and price, but which side of the

76
00:04:26,274 --> 00:04:29,969
market, the volume that traded occurred, the bid side or the offer side.

77
00:04:30,410 --> 00:04:34,370
So, here you see a picture of the market depth.

78
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:38,010
So, you see there's 280 on the bid. There's 565 on the offer.

79
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:41,250
The market is currently bid 913.25.

80
00:04:41,530 --> 00:04:43,630
It's currently offered at 913.5.

81
00:04:44,550 --> 00:04:48,590
Below the bid at 913, even there's 722 lots.

82
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:53,370
Above the offer at 913.75, there's 893 lots.

83
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:56,930
If you are working a bid, if say

84
00:04:56,930 --> 00:04:59,100
you're trying to buy it at 913.25 and

85
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:03,750
you're on the bid, you're part of the 280 lots there, you're considered a passive buyer.

86
00:05:04,370 --> 00:05:07,467
If you're trying to sell at 913.50,

87
00:05:07,467 --> 00:05:10,564
you are on the offer at 1913.50.

88
00:05:10,564 --> 00:05:16,759
You're part of that size of 565 there. You are a passive seller.

89
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:28,450
If you get tired of waiting on the offer at 1913.50, you move your price down to 1913.25. You are being aggressive.

90
00:05:28,650 --> 00:05:32,390
You are going to the buyer's price where they're sitting on the bid.

91
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:34,910
So the guy that's sitting on

92
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:37,430
the bid, he's passive, but you

93
00:05:37,430 --> 00:05:39,530
moving your price down from

94
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:42,890
1913.5 down to 1913.25, you're being aggressive. You're the aggressor.

95
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:55,580
A common problem that many losing traders face is they focus purely on technical indicators which lag the market.

96
00:05:56,560 --> 00:06:00,220
Indicators are derived off of price and are based on what the market did in the past.

97
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,697
Consistently profitable traders

98
00:06:01,697 --> 00:06:03,093
don't lag the market. They

99
00:06:03,093 --> 00:06:08,678
don't get into the trend at the end of the move. They get in at the beginning of new trends.

100
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,570
And what order flow will

101
00:06:11,570 --> 00:06:13,600
do for you, it'll help you determine

102
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,920
when the trends are beginning. It'll help you

103
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,950
also see when they end, but it's

104
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:19,980
not telling you to get in at

105
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:28,680
the end because you'll know that it's ending. And if anything, you can tell if the market is going to go sideways or a new trend is going to happen.

